This product includes software developed as part of the 2026 MoonBit Hackathon
(November season, second quarterly round).

Portions of the reference implementation in tools/reference_crdt.py follow the
standard definitions of G-Counter, PN-Counter, OR-Set (add-wins) and
LWW-Register as described in:

  N. Preguiça, M. Shapiro et al., "A comprehensive study of Convergent and
  Commutative Replicated Data Types", INRIA RR-7506, 2011.

  M. Kleppmann, "Designing Data-Intensive Applications", O'Reilly, 2017, ch. 5.

No source code was copied from those publications; the implementations were
written from the definitions.
